{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"feathered-ironclad-macaque","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe Gerrit Verify matrix runs the same default-tier selection on Ubuntu Python 3.11, 3.12, and 3.13. Every cell currently enables pytest-cov and independently enforces the same repository-wide fail-under floor. All three cells remain necessary for supported-Python behavioral and contractual compatibility, but duplicate coverage instrumentation may occupy scarce runners without adding a distinct gate. The closed ropeable-hydrated-siskin ticket established the accepted precedent of retaining platform tests while collecting coverage only where it adds a unique verdict.\n\n## Plan\n- Attribute coverage overhead with paired same-host runs and current GitHub step timings; inspect version-conditional production paths and prove the matrix selection remains identical.\n- Compare current practice in at least three popular, actively maintained OSS projects and search tracker history for acceptance or rejection.\n- Add a held-out workflow contract test that requires every Ubuntu Python cell to keep running both pytest tiers while exactly one primary Ubuntu cell collects coverage and enforces fail-under.\n- Change only the coverage condition in .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml so Ubuntu Python 3.13 remains the coverage gate and Python 3.11/3.12 execute the identical tests without tracing.\n- Run a defect-seeded mutation of the condition, focused workflow tests, lint, and typecheck; then land through Gerrit and measure runner-seconds saved on the resulting Verify run.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A runtime experiment isolates coverage instrumentation cost from test selection and reports per-cell and summed runner-time savings.\n- [ ] The three Ubuntu Python versions and macOS cell execute the same test selections as before; no test, assertion, marker tier, or external boundary is removed or moved.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.13 still collects branch coverage and enforces the existing fail-under threshold.\n- [ ] A workflow contract test fails if coverage is enabled on zero or multiple Ubuntu matrix cells, or if either pytest tier is removed from any cell.\n- [ ] At least three popular, actively maintained OSS projects are cited, and the remediation meets the umbrella consensus rule.\n- [ ] Tracker history is cited, including ropeable-hydrated-siskin and any prior rejection.\n- [ ] Focused tests, lint, typecheck, Gerrit LLM-Review +1, and Gerrit Verified +1 pass before merge.\n- [ ] The merged Verify run quantifies aggregate Ubuntu runner-seconds saved without claiming parallel matrix time as critical-path wall time.\n- [ ] Back-out is a Gerrit revert restoring coverage flags on all Ubuntu cells.","id":"1ec4-d7e9-b1f1-40c3","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["ci","performance","coverage"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Collect coverage once on the primary Ubuntu CI cell"},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786702763209295001,"uuid":"6e776abd-0bd9-46b3-bf38-1dd50b9cfc6a"}